Not correct.  The two scenarios in the book were: (a) alien invation; or (b)
technological singularity.  It was made ambiguous in the book, but in the 
afterword - in the "Analog" version I read, and in what he's written elsewhere 
(Whole Earth Review) and other places he believes (b) is coming.  You should read
what he actually says about the subject.

As to godhood, that is a matter of definition.  To most of our ancestors we 
already have the powers of gods.  

>Discussion...?

Obviously I cannot prove that the singularity will occur; but I have stated my
reasons for believing that it will.  So any discussion would be more academic 
than practical.  But if you really want to discuss it - and 
the tone of some of your remarks leaves me in doubt - then I'm game.  But your
arguments so far seem poorly thought out and full of arbitrary assertions with 
no supporting evidence. 

