A driving, periodic force wouldn't necessarily cause a catastrophic 
resonance. In fact, many complex systems become more chaotic when 
subjected to such forces. But if all people born in the same month had 
some similarities, month dependent diseases would be a possibility.

Personally I think there is a strong argument against astrology that it
isn't more obvious. If there really were some sort of periodic influence
from the movements of the planets, it would be an evolutionary advantage
for living beings to exploit it (as we learn from artificial life, vitoid
systems seems to be very good at finding and exploiting any kind of bugs).
For example, if Venus had anything to do with the success of
pair-relations, evolution would lead to pair-formation linked to the
position of Venus. We would get an ecology with clear astrological
patterns (attempts to oust the old pack-leaders by younger males would
tend to take place when Mars was in a favorable conjunction and Jupiter
and Saturn in unfavorable, etc.). As far as I know, there are no such 
correlations (except with the Moon and Sun, which have other, more 
obvious explanations). 

